25,2,1,talk,May,,"It seems some old ideas actually worked. One pilot was technically sound, and another met its cost targets.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"We have a problem. The late-turn pool is thin, and we're relying heavily on overtime for both departures and maintenance.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Interestingly, the delays aren't where we think. It's the connections that cost time, not the actual travel or the ticketing machines.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I've found that pre-war shells are risky due to unrecorded voids, and the ferry and rail offices haven't agreed on data terms.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The budget is tight. Operating subsidies are trimmed, and ticketing fees are now costing us more than our road resurfacing.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, if the pool is that thin, does that make any expansion of hours impossible?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,It makes it very risky. We are already under-established on roadway and signals crews.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, if ticketing fees are so high, would a single platform help the budget?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, did those accessibility records show if the lane-priority projects actually lasted?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"It might, but we have to consider the initial capital cost and the current ledger balances.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,May,,"Actually, some lane-priority stretches were returned to mixed traffic. It didn't all stick.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Midori, if the issue is connections, perhaps a more streamlined corridor is better than just adding hours.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Midori,,"That's a fair point. The mid-city runs are slower now, even if the platforms clear at the same rate.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I'm concerned about any plan involving those old station shells; the contingency costs are becoming prohibitive.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I noticed a ring-fenced construction balance from a lapsed grant. We might have specific funds available for certain works.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,May,,We should avoid repeating the mistakes of the lane-priority failures.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,And we certainly can't ignore the staffing freeze's impact on the rosters.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Midori,,It sounds like we need something that addresses the connection delays without overstretching the crews.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Shizue,,And something that doesn't require complex agreements between the ferry and rail back offices.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,Let's see the candidates and see which one fits these constraints.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
